2026-09-23 00:34:30,230 | INFO | [public-fetch] [agents] name=bull mode=backtesting model=gemini-3.5-flash-lite cache_hit=False tokens_in=17768 tokens_out=319 tokens_cached_in=12105 tokens_uncached_in=5663 tokens_thinking=0 tokens_total=18087 latency_ms=1758 first_event_latency_ms=1758 tool_calls=0 observability_warnings=1 summary='Based on the provided U.S. House of Representatives Periodic Transaction Report (PTR) under the STOCK Act (PDF URL: `https://disclosures-clerk.house.gov/public_disc/ptr-pdfs/2026/20033725.pdf`), here is the bull case argument for the key companies and transactions disclosed in the filing:  1. **Alphabet Inc. (GOOGL)** & **Amazon.com, Inc. (AMZN)**: Sustained institutional and congressional confidence in mega-cap technology leaders, driven by durable cloud computing infrastructure growth, artificial intelligence adoption, and resilient digital advertising and e-commerce cash flows. 2. **NVIDIA Corporation (NVDA)**: Highlighting ongoing conviction in accelerated computing, AI data center hardware infrastructure, and robust long-term enterprise demand. 3. **The Walt Disney Company (DIS)**: Optimism regarding operational turnarounds in streaming profitability, parks and experiences resilience, and monetization of premium media content. 4. **Vistra Corp. (VST)**: Participation reflecting powerful secular tailwinds in electrical power generation and utility infrastructure, heavily catalyzed by surging data center and AI energy consumption. 5. **PayPal Holdings, Inc. (PYPL)** & **Tempus AI, Inc. (TEM)**: Selective allocation toward high-growth fintech innovation and healthcare artificial intelligence diagnostics.  *Note: As instructed, no orders are submitted.*  RESULT: Argued the bull case for the companies disclosed in the congressional Periodic Transaction Report without executing any trades.' trace=/Users/robertgrzesik/Library/Caches/lumibot/1.0/agent_runtime/traces/bull/57e4863f92702b72fc779986ea40203b299162059dcc152c13dd9843bc6af87b-202609